In $ eta^{-}$ decay a neutron changes to a proton, emitting an electron and an antineutrino: $$n ightarrow p + e^{-} +  ar{
u}_{e}$$. The presence of $ ar{
u}$ in $$Q ightarrow R + X +  ar{
u}$$ tells you this is $ eta^{-}$ decay, so X must be the $ eta^{-}$ particle, which is an electron.

